---
/**
 * Yolk Post's privacy policy (the Android game). Linked from Google Play and from the game.
 * Facts come from build 1.0.0: progress is saved only on the device; the game itself has no server and no
 * analytics; the two outside services are the Google Mobile Ads SDK (between-delivery and optional rewarded
 * ads, requested as child-directed, under the age of consent, non-personalised, rating G) and Google Play
 * Billing (one optional purchase). The advertising-ID permission is removed from the app's manifest.
 * If the build changes (analytics, accounts, another SDK), this page must change first.
 */
import LegalLayout from '../../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../../lib/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'who', label: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'summary', label: 'In short' },
  { id: 'device', label: 'Saved on your device' },
  { id: 'ads', label: 'Ads' },
  { id: 'purchase', label: 'The one purchase' },
  { id: 'children', label: 'Children' },
  { id: 'permissions', label: 'Permissions' },
  { id: 'delete', label: 'Deleting your data' },
  { id: 'rights', label: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Yolk Post privacy policy"
  description="How the Yolk Post platformer for Android handles data: progress stays on your phone, no accounts, no analytics, child-safe ads from Google AdMob and one optional purchase through Google Play."
  updated="21 November 2026"
  toc={toc}
  crumbs={[
    { href: '/', label: 'Home' },
    { href: '/games', label: 'Games' },
    { href: '/games/yolk-post', label: 'Yolk Post' },
    { label: 'Privacy policy' },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    This policy covers <strong>Yolk Post</strong>, our platform game for Android (Google Play package
    <code>com.ismailapps.yolkpost</code>). It explains what data the game handles, why, and what you can do about it. The
    website has its own <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="who">Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    Yolk Post is made by IsmailApps, the name under which {site.founder.legalName} publishes software and games. It is not a
    registered company yet. The person responsible for your data (the controller) is:
  </p>
  <address>
    {site.founder.legalName}<br />
    {site.founder.postalAddress}<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
  </address>

  <h2 id="summary">In short</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>There are <strong>no accounts</strong>, no sign-in, no chat and no way to share personal information in the game.</li>
    <li>Your progress is saved <strong>only on your phone</strong>. We never receive it.</li>
    <li>We use <strong>no analytics and no tracking</strong>.</li>
    <li>
      The game uses two outside services: <strong>Google AdMob</strong> for ads, requested as directed to children (no
      advertising ID, no personalised ads), and <strong>Google Play</strong> for one optional purchase.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="device">Saved on your device</h2>
  <p>
    The game keeps save files on your phone with your progress: deliveries done, stamps, lost parcels found, badges, the
    caps and plasters you unlocked, which story pages you have seen, whether you own the full route, a count of finished
    deliveries (so ads keep to their limits), and your settings (music, sound, vibration, reduced shake, button size and
    side). They stay in the game's private storage on your device. We have no server for them, and the game does not send
    them anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ads">Ads (Google AdMob)</h2>
  <p>
    In the free version, a short ad can appear between some deliveries: never during play, never right after a crack, not in
    your first few deliveries or first minutes of play, and at most one every three deliveries. You can also choose to watch
    a video for a reward, such as skipping a delivery you are stuck on. Owning the full route removes the ads between
    deliveries.
  </p>
  <p>
    The ads are provided by Google's Mobile Ads SDK (Google AdMob). Every ad request from Yolk Post is marked as
    <strong>directed to children and under the age of consent</strong>, asks for <strong>non-personalised</strong> ads only,
    and limits the content rating to <strong>G</strong> (general audiences). With these settings, Google does not show
    personalised ads or remarketing. We also removed the advertising ID permission from the app, so the advertising ID is
    not available to it.
  </p>
  <p>
    To show an ad, count it and prevent fraud, the Google Mobile Ads SDK still processes some technical information. Google
    lists this as: the device's IP address (which can indicate a rough location), other device and app identifiers (such as
    the app set ID), how you interact with ads, and diagnostic information such as crashes and performance. It is encrypted
    in transit. Google handles this information under its own policies:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from apps that use its services</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="https://developers.google.com/admob/android/privacy/play-data-disclosure" rel="noopener">What the Google Mobile Ads SDK collects</a>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not receive any of this information about you. We only see totals in our AdMob account, such as how many ads were
    shown.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Legal basis:</strong> showing non-personalised ads to fund a free game is our legitimate interest (Art. 6(1)(f)
    GDPR). Buying the full route removes the ads between deliveries, and the reward videos are always optional.
  </p>

  <h2 id="purchase">The one purchase (Google Play)</h2>
  <p>
    World 1 is free. One optional, one-time purchase, the full route, opens every other world. A grown-up check (a
    times-table question) comes before the purchase starts. Payment happens entirely in Google Play: we never see your card
    or payment details. Google tells the game only whether the full route is owned, so it can unlock it and restore it on a
    new phone.
  </p>
  <p>
    For our records, refunds and taxes, Google Play shows us details of each order, such as the order number, date, price
    and country. We use them only for that. Google handles payments under the
    <a href="https://payments.google.com/payments/apis-secure/u/0/get_legal_document?ldo=0&ldt=privacynotice" rel="noopener">Google Payments privacy notice</a>.
  </p>
  <p><strong>Legal basis:</strong> providing what you bought (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR) and keeping records the law requires (Art. 6(1)(c)).</p>

  <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
  <p>
    Yolk Post is made for all ages. We do not ask for, and do not knowingly collect, personal information from anyone,
    including children under 13. The ads are requested in Google's child-directed mode described above, which is designed for
    apps that children may use (including under the US COPPA rule), and the purchase sits behind a grown-up check. If you are
    a parent and have a question, email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="permissions">Permissions</h2>
  <p>
    Yolk Post asks for no permissions that need your approval. Android grants it internet and network-state access, used to
    load ads and to talk to Google Play for the purchase; billing access, for the purchase; and vibration, for small buzzes
    when you land, crack or deliver (you can turn this off in Settings). Google's ads library also uses Android's background-task system
    to send its ad reports. The game does not include the advertising ID permission.
  </p>

  <h2 id="delete">Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>
    Uninstalling the game, or clearing its storage in Android's settings, deletes your progress from the phone. We have no
    copy, so it cannot be restored afterwards. A purchase is linked to your Google account by Google Play, not to us: after
    reinstalling, use <strong>Restore purchase</strong> on the unlock screen to get the full route back.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us about any personal data we hold about you, and ask us to correct or delete it. In practice, from the game
    we hold only Google Play's order records if you bought the full route. For data processed by Google to show ads or take
    payments, Google's policies explain your choices. You can also complain to a data protection supervisory authority. Email
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will reply within a month.
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If the game starts handling data differently, for example a new feature or another service, we will update this page and
    the date at the top before that version is released.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
